{
  "id": "murphy-shakti-fibonacci-hippocampus",
  "name": "Shakti: Fibonacci and hippocampus, 4 phases (about 20 min)",
  "category": "signals",
  "evidence": "claim",
  "origin": "Todd Murphy, 8 Coil Shakti software (the vendor says the design was 'used in the lab in unpublished studies')",
  "uT": 1,
  "summary": "Murphy's 4-phase 8 Coil Shakti session over both temporal lobes: a Fibonacci-amplitude signal (4 min) and the standard hippocampal 'LTP' signal (5.25 min) take turns twice, an alternation meant to keep the brain from habituating to one signal. The vendor calls it 'less well-tested'.",
  "setting": "Dark, quiet room, eyes closed; relax without meditating or falling asleep. The vendor says to start with the coils over the temporal lobes.",
  "schedule": "Vendor rules: at most once a week or every 72 h, never on consecutive days; a series of up to 6 sessions, then a 21-day break.",
  "notes": "Phases as on the vendor page: Fibonacci 4 min, hippocampus 5.25 min, Fibonacci 4 min, hippocampus 5.25 min (18.5 min of signal; the vendor calls it a 20-min session), with abrupt switches. All 8 coils sit in the 8 Coil Shakti's 4-coil cross over each temporal lobe (front FT7/FT8, top C5/C6, back TP7/TP8, bottom T9/T10; the vendor gives the cross as a chart and photos without 10-10 names, so these sites are an inference). The Shakti's paired +/- coils and its channel alternation are not reproduced (no alternation setting is given for this session); all coils play the same signal together. The vendor says only that in the Fibonacci signal 'the magnetic field goes up and down in strength at each Fibonacci node'; the file is proprietary. It is approximated by the project's Fibonacci table: theta bursts (4 pulses at 100 Hz, 5 bursts a second, after the Larson & Lynch 1986 LTP timing) whose amplitudes rise 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13, 21 and fall back over 3 s, repeated without a pause (the page does not say whether this signal has the Shakti's 4-s latency). The hippocampal 'LTP' file is proprietary. It is approximated on the vendor's standard 3-ms points: 4 bursts of 4 biphasic pulses 9 ms apart, one burst every 186 ms (5.4 Hz, the spectral peak the vendor reports for its LTP signal), then the standard 4 s of silence (about 9.4 s of field per minute; the vendor gives 9.6 s). Murphy says the hippocampal signal is more likely to have positive effects over the right side or both sides, but not over the left side alone (his right-side rule goes back to one small Persinger-lab study, Persinger, Richards & Koren 1994: right-sided LTP-pattern fields were rated more pleasant). The vendor reports headache or pressure in about 2% of users with hippocampal signals; if so, lower the intensity by one third. Not for people with epilepsy or a seizure history; stop at once on fear or any distress. Independent double-blind tests found no effect of God-Helmet-type fields (Granqvist 2005; Gendle & McGrath 2012).",
  "targets": ["left-hippocampus-head", "left-hippocampus-body", "left-hippocampus-tail", "right-hippocampus-head", "right-hippocampus-body", "right-hippocampus-tail"],
